  "summary": "RemControl is an Android banking trojan distributed as a fake TVTap IPTV app dropper that suppresses Google Play Protect via a local VPN, signs its payload per installation, and abuses the Accessibility Service to inject C2-served phishing overlays, stream the screen, log keystrokes and capture lock patterns. It resolves its C2 through a Telegram dead-drop (AES-128-CBC keyed by the marker string 'numeraZZZas') and talks to a FastAPI 'RemControl Proxy' backend over WebSocket with an HTTP /api fallback. Samples are branded with the hardcoded affiliate tag UNKK and geography campaign tags such as IT-NEW and FR-NEW4.",
